<handout>
    <title>Knowledge Check LT 1-3</title>
<exercise>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            Tell the story of rainfall over several minutes.  Label the axes.
        </p>
   
    <figure>
     <image source="speed4.png" width="35%">
        <shortdescription>a qualitative graph that starts at the origin and increases, then decreases to the x-axis, and finally increases again.</shortdescription>
     </image>
    </figure>
</introduction>
<answer>
        <p>
            The rainfall increased at a steady rate for several minutes.  It then started to rain less and less, at a steady rate, until it stopped for a few minutes.  The rainfall began to increase at a steady rate again.
        </p>
    </answer>

   
        <p>
            Sketch the graph of the amount of money in an account over several months according to these parameters:

        </p>
        <ul> 
            <li>
                <p>
                    Your money stays steady for a few months.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Your money grows greatly within one month.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Your money grows greatly within one month.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    What is the independent variable?  Label the graph.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    What is the dependent variable?  Label the graph.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
        <figure>
            <image source="q1.png" width="35%">
                <shortdescription>A first quadrant graph with a short decreasing line segment up on the y-axis</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </figure>
    
    <answer>
        <p>
            The independent variable is months, and the dependent variable is amount of money.
        </p>
        <figure>
            <image source="q1b.png">
                <shortdescription>A first quadrant graph that starts high on the y-axis and decreases, then is horizontal for a short time, followed by a steep decrease, almost to the x-axis.  The graph ends with a horizontal line at this point,</shortdescription>
            </image>
            </figure>
    </answer>
    <figure>
        <image source="case3.png">
            <shortdescription>A 3 figure pattern.  Figure 1 is an x shape made up of 5 boxes, figure 2 is the same shape with 9 boxes, and figure 3 is the same shape with 13 boxes.</shortdescription>
        </image>
    </figure>
    <p>
       Does the pattern follow a linear pattern?  Explain how you know. 
    </p> 
    <p>
        What is the rule for the pattern?  Show your work.
    </p>
    <p>
        How many boxes are in the 55th figure?  Show your work or explain your thinking.
    </p> 
 <answer>
    <p>
        The pattern is linear because 4 boxes are added each time.
    </p>
    <p>
        The rule is 4x+1   The constant change (common difference) of 4 is the coefficent on the variable, and subtracting 4 (opposite operation going backward) from the first figure 5, results in the inital value (when x = 0) of 1, which is the constant.    
    </p>
    <p>
        4(55)+1=221 boxes in the 55th figure.
    </p>

    </answer>   
</exercise>
</handout>